{"id":"word:hebrew:H6664","type":"word","title":"צֶדֶק","subtitle":"H6664 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the right (natural, moral or legal); also (abstractly) equity or (figuratively) prosperity","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to צֶדֶק (H6664) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 119 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"צֶדֶק (tsedeq) means the right (natural, moral or legal); also (abstractly) equity or (figuratively) prosperity First listed occurrence: Dan 9 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"צֶדֶק","transliteration":"tsedeq","pronunciation":"tseh'-dek","strong":"H6664","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6664","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["צֶ֑דֶק","צֶ֖דֶק","צֶ֣דֶק","צֶ֔דֶק","צֶֽדֶק"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",63],["HR/Ncmsa",14],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",10],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",6],["HC/Ncmsa",5],["HNcmsc",3],["HTd/Ncmsa",3],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",3],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",3],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp1cs",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"the right (natural, moral or legal); also (abstractly) equity or (figuratively) prosperity","usage":"× even, (× that which is altogether) just(-ice), (un-)right(-eous) (cause, -ly, -ness).","full":"H6664. tsedeq צֶ֫דֶק noun masculine Isa 1:21 rightness, righteousness ; — ׳צ Lev 19:36 87t.; צִדְקִי Isa 41:10 8 t., etc.; — 1 what is right, just, normal; rightness, justness , of weights and measures, וָצֶדֶק שְׁלֵמָה אֶבֶן אֵיפָה, Deut 25:15 a perfect and a just weight, ephah ; צ ׳מאֹזְנֵי ; צ ׳בַּת צ, ׳הִין צ, ׳אֵיפַת צ, ׳אַבְנֵי Lev 19:36 (H) Job 31:6 ; Ezek 45:10 ; צ ׳מַעְגְּלֵי right paths Psa 23:3 ; צ ׳זִבְחֵי right peace-offerings Deut 33:19 ; Psa 4:6 ; Psalm 51:21. 2 righteousness , in government: a. of judges, rulers, kings , בצ ׳שׁפט Lev 19:15 (H); צ ׳שׁפט Deut 1:16 ; Prov 31:9 ; צ ׳משׁפט Deut 16:18 ; צ ׳רדף 16:20 ; צ ׳חוֺקֵק Prov 8:15 ; לצ ׳מלך Isa 32:1 ; צ ׳דבּר Psa 58:2 ; also Prov 25:5 ; Psa 94:15 ; Eccl 5:7 . b. of law, as מִשְׁמָּטִים Isa 58:2 ; Psa 119:7 ; 119:62 ; 119:75 ; 119:106 ; 119:160 ( ᵐ5 , but מִשְׁמַּט ᵑ0 ), 119:164 ; as עֵדוֺת 119:138 ; 119:144 ; as מִצְוֺר 119:172 . c. of Davidic king, Messiah Isa 11:4-5 , 16:5 ; Psa 45:5 , דצ ׳דין 72:2 . d. of Jerusalem, as seat of just government , הַצֶּדֶק עִיר Isa 1:26 city of righteousness ; צ ׳נְוֵה Jer 31:23 ; 50:7 (possibly these reflect an original god צֶדֶק , see צֶדֶק מַלְכִּי ); ׳צ בָּהּ יָלִין Isa 1:21 righteousness used to lodge in her ; compare הצ ׳מְקוֺם Eccl 3:16 the place of righteousness. e. of God's attribute as sovereign Job 36:3 , husband of Israel Hosea 2:21 ; ׳צ his personified agent Psa 85:11 ; 85:12 ; Psalm 85:14, foundation of his throne 89:15 = 97:2 ; in his government 9:9 ; 65:6 ; 96:13 = 98:9 , promise Isa 45:19 , administration of justice Job 8:3 ; Jer 11:20 ; Psalm 7:18; Psa 48:11 ; 50:6 = 97:6 , vindication of his people 9:5 ; 35:24 ; 35:28 ; raising up Cyrus Isa 45:13 , calling his servant 42:6 ; צִדְקִי אֱלֹהֵי Psa 4:2 God of my righteousness (who vindicates me); his ׳צ is everlasting 119:142 . 3 righteousness, justice , in a case or cause Job 6:29 ; 8:6 ; 29:14 ; Psa 35:27 ; Isa 59:4 ; God כצ ׳שׁפט Psa 7:9 judges according to righteousness ; כצ ׳גמל 18:21 ; כצ ׳השׁיב 18:25 ; צ ׳שׁמע 17:1 צ ׳הוציא 37:6 . 4 rightness , in speech, צ ׳דבּר Psa 52:5 (opposed to שֶׁקֶר ); צ ׳יַגִּיד Prov 12:17 ; ׳בצ פי אמרי כל 8:8 ; צ ׳שִׂפְתֵי 16:13 . 5 righteousness , as ethically right Job 35:2 ; Psa 17:15 ; 45:8 ; Prov 1:3 ; 2:9 ; Eccl 7:15 ; Jer 22:13 ; Ezek 3:20 ; Hosea 10:12 (read צ ׳מְּרִי , so ᵐ5 We Now); עלמים׳צ Dan 9:24 ; צ ׳עשׂה Isa 64:4 ; Psa 119:121 ; צ ׳פעל 15:2 ; צ ׳למד Isa 26:6 , 10 ; צ ׳בקּשׁ Zeph 2:3 ; צ ׳רדף Isa 51:1 ; צ ׳ידע 51:7 . 6 righteousness as vindicated, justification in controversy with enemies and troubles, deliverance, victory, prosperity: a. of God as covenant-keeping, in redemption , צִדְקִי בִּימִין Isa 41:10 , || יֵשַׁע 45:8 ; 51:5 , compare 42:21 ; צ ׳בשּׂר Psa 40:10 ; צ ׳אִמְרַת 119:123 . b. in name צִדְקֵנוּ יהוה , of Messianic king (vindicating people's cause and giving victory) Jer 23:6 ; of city 33:16 . c. of people as enjoying ׳צ of salvation, || יְשׁוּעָה Isa 62:1 ; || כָּבוֺד 58:8 ; 62:2 ; צ יִלְבְּשׁוּ ׳כהנים Psa 132:9 ; צ ׳שַׁעֲרֵי 118:19 ; הצ ׳אֵילֵי Isa 61:3 . d. of Cyrus , ׳צ לְרַגְלוֺ יִקְרָאֵהוּ Isa 41:2 (who) in victory calleth him at every step (Che Hpt on whose steps attends victory , so Di Du).","rootNote":"from 6663 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Dan 9 24","keyReferences":["Dan 9 24","Deut 1 16","Deut 16 18","Deut 16 20","Deut 16 20","Deut 25 15","Deut 25 15","Deut 33 19"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":119,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Dan 9 24","book":"Dan","chapter":9,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶ֣דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"Deut 1 16","book":"Deut","chapter":1,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶ֔דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 16 18","book":"Deut","chapter":16,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶֽדֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 16 20","book":"Deut","chapter":16,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶ֥דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 16 20","book":"Deut","chapter":16,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶ֖דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 25 15","book":"Deut","chapter":25,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/צֶ֨דֶק֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 25 15","book":"Deut","chapter":25,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/צֶ֖דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 33 19","book":"Deut","chapter":33,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צֶ֑דֶק","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Eccl 3 16","book":"Eccl","chapter":3,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/צֶּ֖דֶק","sour